# Phaser: Center Modals on Screen

Game uses `scale.mode: Phaser.Scale.ENVELOP` + `autoCenter: CENTER_BOTH`. Phaser `this.add.dom()` coordinates often look off-center on the real viewport.

## Do this for name/input dialogs and full-screen overlays

Use a **fixed HTML overlay on `document.body`**, not Phaser DOMElement:

```ts
const wrapper = document.createElement('div');
wrapper.style.cssText = 'position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:9999;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;';
// append panel inside wrapper, then:
document.body.appendChild(wrapper);
// on close: wrapper.remove()
```

Reference implementation: `CoverScene.showNameInput()` / `submitNameForm()`.

## Avoid

- `this.add.dom(width/2, height/2)` + absolute `left/top` offsets for “centering”
- Assuming game-world center == browser viewport center under ENVELOP

## Cleanup

Always `remove()` the overlay when submitting or leaving the scene so it doesn’t stick after scene changes.
